{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>A serpent.</b> It is a נָחָשׁ; and I say that it is so called on account of that it hisses (נוֹשֵׁף), as in ״וְאַתָּה תְּשׁוּפֶנּוּ עָקֵב״ (Genesis 3)." "<b>That bites the horse's heels.</b> Such is the way of a serpent, and he likened him to a serpent that bites the heels of a horse — <b>so that his rider falls backward</b> — without having touched him. And its parallel we find in Samson: ״וַיִּלְפֹּת שִׁמְשׁוֹן אֶת שְׁנֵי עַמּוּדֵי הַתָּוֶךְ״ and so on (Judges 16) — and those on the roof died; and Onkelos translated כְּחִוֵּי חוּרְמָן — the name of a species of serpent for whose bite there is no cure, and it is the צִפְעוֹנִי, and it is called חוּרְמָן on account of that it renders everything חֵרֶם; and וּכְפִיתְנָא — like פֶּתֶן; יִכְמוֹן — lies in wait."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:12.625578477Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}